What is JSON format?

JSON stands for:

JavaScript Object Notation

It is a simple text format used to store and exchange data between applications.

Example
{
  "name": "Sugumar",
  "business": "AI Consultant",
  "city": "Chennai"
}

Here:

"name" = Key
"Sugumar" = Value

So the structure is:

{
  "Key": "Value"
}

=================

What is JSONL format?

JSONL stands for:

JSON Lines

It contains one JSON object per line.

Example JSONL file
{"name":"Sugumar","business":"AI Consultant"}
{"name":"Ravi","business":"Bakery Owner"}
{"name":"Priya","business":"Textile Shop Owner"}

Each line is a separate JSON record.

============


Gemma 2 fine-tuning, JSONL is commonly useful because each line can represent one training example.

